  "owed_measurement_coverage": [
    "Canonical neural inputs must be generated once with identical_wave_prepare_neural.py onNV, transferred viaR2 and hash verified onAMD before starting this plan.",
    "Device-handle grouping and explicit persistent-buffer adapters require separate multi-call scenarios; generic single board calls do not prove those gains.",
    "Cross-vendor aggregation must compare complete matching SHA/arm/plan/data output digests; localhost equality alone is insufficient.",
    "Apple checks are authorized only through root, one GPU job at a time; per-algorithm within-version Apple/host qualification remains required before promotion.",
    "Full neural training and other nonrepresentative workloads excluded from this bounded wave; no whole-catalog claim.",
    "Stored opponent metrics only with exact fixture/params match; do not compare medium timings directly with full-row stored cells."
  ],
  "timing_contract": "board-warm-single-call",
  "measurement_rationale": "Match existing board semantics: one untimed warmup fit/infer, then ONE reported GPU timing sample per ON/OFF arm. Same operation/fixture on both arms. Host ID has no timer and no warmup. Cold-single-call optional is a separate contract; grouped completion needs separate multi-call adapter and is not inferred from these single calls. Store warm/full results are not directly comparable to these medium workloads.",
